[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Independent DC response validation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DC-VALIDATION-ADMISSION-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Validate sparse excitation before provider invocation
STATEMENT: >>>
Sparse excitation shall have exactly the matrix dimension and finite components.
Either violation alone shall return InvalidInput before invoking a provider.
Dense provider responses shall have exactly the matrix dimension and finite
components; violations shall be classified as NumericalFailure.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: sparse_rhs_shape_and_finiteness_fail_independently_before_provider_calls
uses a tripwire provider; dense_provider_response_requires_exact_shape_and_finite_components
checks malformed response vectors through the public independent validator.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DC-VALIDATION-SCALE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Retain finite componentwise backward-error evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
Independent DC verification shall normalize the residual by absolute RHS plus
absolute coefficient-times-solution contributions. A finite accumulated residual
shall not hide overflow of its absolute scale. Nonrepresentable validation
evidence shall return NumericalFailure rather than a successful zero error.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: cancellation_does_not_hide_overflow_of_the_absolute_residual_scale
uses finite cancelling terms with an overflowing absolute sum. The scalar
reference delta/(12+delta) in row_scaling_preserves_the_independent_scalar_backward_error
is checked under64 exact power-of-two row scalings, Proptest seed2026111925.
This verifies the validator, not arbitrary provider conditioning or convergence.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: DC-VALIDATION-BOUNDARY-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve inclusive componentwise acceptance
STATEMENT: >>>
The existing DC componentwise backward-error limit of1e-10 shall be inclusive;
a representably greater error shall fail with NumericalFailure.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: exact_backward_error_limit_is_inclusive_but_the_next_solution_is_not
constructs exact half-integer RHS and solution values with residual1 and scale
10^10, then increases the solution by one representable step. This preserves
the existing policy and does not introduce a new physical signal tolerance.
<<<
